    function automatic int queue_pop_coupler_SPOOL_UP(
        int ASYNC,
        int CONFLICT_PROOF,
        int REGISTERED_IN,
        int REGISTERED_IN_BRAM,
        int REGISTERED_OUT_BRAM
    );
        // +1 to assert pop
        // + read latency to fetch data
        if(ASYNC == 1) return (1 + queue_async_READ_LATENCY(REGISTERED_OUT_BRAM));
        return (1 + queue_READ_LATENCY(CONFLICT_PROOF, REGISTERED_IN, REGISTERED_IN_BRAM, REGISTERED_OUT_BRAM));
    endfunction
"
- correct arguments passed in
- correct arguments passed into 'queue_READ_LATENCY()' and 'queue_async_READ_LATENCY()'
- from the time that ready is asserted, it takes one cycle to assert pop, then the respective read latency
  - so its 1 + respective sync/async read latency 
